    delphi:hasConfidence "0.84"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The prediction maps directly to standard enrichment tests on large public resources. Appropriate matched null models can test whether overlap is specific rather than a consequence of broadly studied, pleiotropic genes." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Define independent morphogenesis and learning-memory gene sets, test overlap against degree-, annotation-, and expression-matched null sets, and assess enrichment of memory genes in cancer, regeneration, and embryogenesis screens." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Annotation circularity and pleiotropy can inflate overlap.", "Gene-set definitions and background universe must be preregistered." ;
